# DHU Backup — EXAMPLE watchlist. This file is never installed.
#
# The installed copy lives at /Library/DHU/backup/etc/watchlist.conf and is the
# ONLY source of watched roots. Write it at install time:
#
#     sudo bash src/install.sh --watch repo=/Users/you/Projects/my-repo
#     sudo bash src/install.sh --watchlist ./my-watchlist.conf
#
# There is deliberately no default watchlist. A default would name directories
# that do not exist on this machine, and the installer would then print OK over
# a store that protects nothing.
#
# Format:  <root-id>  <absolute-path>
# One entry per line; `#` starts a comment. A single trailing `*` on the LAST
# component is the only glob permitted. `src/dhu_backup_core.py:parse_watchlist`
# is the authority on this format; the installer's checks are a stricter subset.
#
# The installed file is root-owned (0644) and is never derived from the
# database, an environment variable, or anything an agent writes. Review C5: a
# task row's `scratchDir` is authoritative about where a task RAN, not about
# what root should READ, and a path written by the adversary and read by a root
# process that copies what it finds is a general exfiltration primitive.
#
# $TMPDIR is written as the LITERAL path (review M4). Run `echo $TMPDIR` and
# paste the result. A glob like /var/folders/*/*/T/agent-task-* would sweep
# another account's temp directory the day a second account exists — and it is
# refused anyway, because the glob is not in the last component.

# repo       /Users/you/Projects/my-repo
# worktrees  /Users/you/Projects/my-repo/.claude/worktrees/*
# scratch    /var/folders/<xx>/<opaque-hash>/T/agent-task-*
